From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: report readiness to the init system

Tell the init system when adbd is ready: sd_notify(READY=1) when built
with HAVE_SYSTEMD, otherwise a byte written to the FIFO named in
$ADBD_READY_FIFO, if set (opened non-blocking, so adbd never waits on a
reader that has given up). Only the first call does anything.

On USB, the right moment is once the USB thread has written the
functionfs descriptors and registered the transport: the gadget's UDC
must not be bound before then, or the bind is silently dropped and the
host never reaches CONFIGURED. usb_init() only starts that thread, so
an adbd on USB signals from there; otherwise adbd_main() signals before
entering its event loop.

Upstream-Status: Pending

AI-Generated: Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/adb.h
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/adb.h
@@ -255,3 +255,9 @@ bool is_usb_enabled();
 #endif
 
 void usb_init();
+#if !ADB_HOST
+// Tell whoever started adbd that it is ready: sd_notify(READY=1) with systemd,
+// otherwise a byte to the FIFO named in $ADBD_READY_FIFO if set. Only the first
+// call does anything.
+void adbd_notify_ready();
+#endif
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -45,6 +45,12 @@
 #include "selinux/android.h"
 #endif
 
+#if defined(HAVE_SYSTEMD)
+#include <systemd/sd-daemon.h>
+#endif
+
+#include <mutex>
+
 #include "adb.h"
 #include "adb_auth.h"
 #include "adb_listeners.h"
@@ -185,6 +191,27 @@ static void drop_privileges() {
 }
 #endif
 
+void adbd_notify_ready() {
+    static std::once_flag once;
+    std::call_once(once, [] {
+#if defined(HAVE_SYSTEMD)
+        sd_notify(1, "READY=1");
+#else
+        const char* ready_fifo = getenv("ADBD_READY_FIFO");
+        if (ready_fifo != nullptr && *ready_fifo != '\0') {
+            // O_NONBLOCK: with no reader, open() fails with ENXIO rather than
+            // blocking this thread for ever; the reader has given up and
+            // gone ahead without the signal.
+            int fd = adb_open(ready_fifo, O_WRONLY | O_NONBLOCK | O_CLOEXEC);
+            if (fd >= 0) {
+                TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY(adb_write(fd, "1\n", 2));
+                adb_close(fd);
+            }
+        }
+#endif
+    });
+}
+
 static void setup_adb(const std::vector<std::string>& addrs) {
 #if defined(__ANDROID__)
     // Get the first valid port from addrs and register it with mDNS.
@@ -311,6 +338,12 @@ int adbd_main() {
     init_jdwp();
     D("adbd_main(): post init_jdwp()");
 
+    // On USB, readiness is signalled from the USB thread once functionfs is
+    // serviced; usb_init() has only started that thread.
+    if (!is_usb) {
+        adbd_notify_ready();
+    }
+
     D("Event loop starting");
     fdevent_loop();
 
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb.cpp
@@ -786,6 +786,12 @@ static void usb_ffs_open_thread() {
                 std::move(control), std::move(bulk_out), std::move(bulk_in),
                 std::move(destruction_notifier)));
         register_transport(transport);
+
+        // functionfs descriptors are written and ep0 is being serviced, so the
+        // gadget will now handle FUNCTIONFS_BIND: this is the moment the UDC
+        // may be bound. Binding earlier races this setup, and the bind is
+        // silently dropped.
+        adbd_notify_ready();
         future.wait();
     }
 }
